;; The webhook incident — 41 customers charged and never provisioned.
;;
;; These are RECORDS, not prose. The whole point of the reconciliation lane is
;; that "who was charged and never got access" is a datalog query over
;; :S.Customer/* datoms — a wiki page listing 41 accounts would be a document
;; ABOUT the company, and it would go stale the moment a credit was booked.
;;
;; The company and every account here are invented. Any resemblance to a real
;; business is accidental.
;;
;; FIGURES READ AS REAL, NOT IMPRESSIVE. 41 accounts at 29/79/149 dollars is a
;; six-person SaaS having a bad morning; 400 accounts and six figures is a
;; company nobody in the room believes exists. Exposure is 272 900 cents
;; ($2 729.00) over the 41 — see is.simm.ops.reconciliation/exposure, which
;; computes it rather than reading it from here.
;;
;; Money is minor units (long cents). Never a float: 0.1 + 0.2 is not 0.3, and
;; this number gets posted into a double-entry ledger.
;;
;; Timestamps are explicit ISO-8601, never (Date.) — the same rule as
;; is.simm.demo.scenario. A wall-clock fixture makes the timeline different on
;; every run and breaks both the 09:00 time-travel beat and any assertion about
;; ordering.

